# SDLC Lifecycle

Every agentic unit of work follows six phases:

1. Research: recall prior context and read the authoritative docs/code.
2. Design: choose an approach with trade-offs and owner-visible rationale.
3. Plan: express acceptance criteria, dependencies, and evidence needs.
4. Implement: change code and docs together when behavior changes.
5. Verify: run quality evidence and review against the relevant protocol.
6. Promote or close: record outcomes, memory, docs status, and active plugin versions.

Short tasks may compress phases, but they must not skip planning evidence,
quality evidence, review judgment, or closeout semantics.
